name air-tanker-orbit
timeout 300

# A FLYING MOVER MUST NOT REPORT BODENKONTAKT — doc/modules/air/module.md §Gaps collision 1, measured.
#
# A unit without an FBFdm yields `AnyWow = true` BY CONSTRUCTION (units/FBSimUnit::BuildMissionSample),
# which is right for a ground position — a launcher really is on the ground — and wrong for a tanker at
# 9 000 m. The bit is not decorative: core/FBMissionMonitor reads it, and a unit that reports weight on
# wheels away from the declared runway is judged to have TOUCHED DOWN OFF THE ASSIGNED RUNWAY and fails
# on its first tick. So this file declares a runway 30 km from the orbit and asks the tanker to fly a
# racetrack for five minutes.
#
# THE MEASUREMENT IS THE VERDICT ITSELF: exit 0 (SUCCESS, the route flown out) means the tanker was
# airborne throughout. With the collision unresolved the same file exits 1 in its first second with
# `touched down off the assigned runway` — one line of difference, and it is FBModule::Airborne(),
# default false, so a ground position's `AnyWow = true` stays correct.
#
# WHAT ELSE THE FILE MEASURES, and it is the second half of the mover contract: the racetrack. `set
# orbit 40000 600` closes a 40 km leg on the inbound bearing; the declared period is the STRAIGHT-LEG
# time budget (the two semicircles add 2*pi*R/v on top), which is stated rather than solved because the
# turn time depends on the speed it would be solving for.
#
# AND A THIRD THING SINCE 2026-07-29: A T0 ROW GETS NO FIRE CONTROL AT ALL. `FBAircraftSpec::CanEmploy`
# is the tier and the armament and nothing else — a row below T2, or a row with no station and no gun,
# never composes a modules/air/FBAirFireControl, so FBState::FireControl is never written for it. That
# is the pilot staffelung of doc/modules/air/module.md §Spec 5 expressed as a member rather than as a
# branch, and it is checkable in one column: over all 1 965 rows of this run `blk_firecontrol` is 0
# (Invalid) and every `fc_*` column holds its "nothing here" value (fc_dlz 0, fc_rng_nm -1,
# fc_gun_err_deg -1). The same columns on air-eagle-amraam.fbm's F-15C read 1 (Valid) and carry a live
# launch zone. A tanker that grew a fire-control computer because the class it shares with a fighter has
# one would be the defect this line guards against.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 with `air ORBIT axisDeg=90 legM=40000 periodS=600` in events.log is the pass.
# Nothing in this file carries a weapon and nothing is meant to die; what a FAILURE looks like is exit 1
# in the first second with a landing verdict on an aeroplane at 9 000 m.

runway 46.84335 6.91523 441.0 228.0 2889

unit shell
  team friendly
  module kc135
  spawn 47.10000 6.40000 9000 90.0 460
  set orbit 40000 600
  wp 47.10000 6.90000 9000 460
